      "title": "Two killed and at least 17 injured as Russia and Ukraine trade blows on power infrastructure",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/18/killed-injured-russia-ukraine-strikes-power-infrastructure",
      "description": "<p>Ukraine used more than 1,000 drones to target Russian oil depots, logistics facilities and datacentres</p><p>Two people have been killed and at least 17 injured as Russia and Ukraine continue to trade strikes on each other’s power infrastructure, after the breakdown of Donald Trump’s short-lived and unilaterally declared “energy ceasefire”.</p><p>One person was killed and 15 wounded overnight after Ukraine used more than 1,000 drones to target Russian oil depots, logistics facilities and datacentres in one of its largest ever aerial bombardments.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/18/killed-injured-russia-ukraine-strikes-power-infrastructure\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-10-18T14:31:30"
    },
    {
      "title": "Blaze at St Petersburg oil sites as Kyiv launches drones at Russia",
      "link": "https://www.business-standard.com/world-news/blaze-at-st-petersburg-oil-sites-as-kyiv-launches-drones-at-russia-126101800383_1.html",
      "description": "Ukrainian attacks set an oil export terminal ablaze in St. Petersburg on Sunday, as Kyiv launched more than 1,000 drones across Russia in one of its largest ever aerial bombardments.\nThe attack comes amid deepening tensions between Ukraine and Washington, with U.S. President Donald Trump criticizing Kyiv for its strikes on Russian oil infrastructure.\nOne person was killed and five more were wounded in the attack, which sparked fires at both the Petersburg Oil Terminal and the city's Ruchi oil depot, said local Gov. Alexander Beglov. A logistics center belonging to Russian retailer Ozon and a data center for local tech giant VK were also targeted, both companies confirmed.\nRussia's Ministry of Defense said Sunday that its forces had destroyed 1,015 Ukrainian drones over 15 Russian regions, as well as the annexed Ukrainian peninsula of Crimea and the Black Sea.\nMeanwhile, a woman died and at least two other people were wounded, including a 6-year-old girl, after Russia launched two .",
      "source_name": "Business Standard Latest",
      "published": "2026-10-18T10:33:12"
    }
